<title>ABU DHABI: UAE firm wins British air force maintenance deal.</title>
<headline>UAE firm wins British air force maintenance deal.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates' Gulf Aircraft Maintenance Company (GAMCO) said on Tuesday it had signed a $47 million contract to service British Royal Air Force's Tristar fleet.</p>
<p>GAMCO said in a statement the five-year contract was signed on February 6.</p>
<p>&quot;The contract covers scheduled and unscheduled aircraft maintenance support for the RAF Tristar L-1011 fleet,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>GAMCO is 60-percent owned by the Abu Dhabi government.</p>
</text>
